{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-989a457b5cd8a821","type":"tool_result","content":"16:**Detailed**: The FMS Guardrails Orchestrator is a Rust service built on axum and tonic that provides a unified REST API for safe AI text generation. It accepts client requests on v1 and v2 API surfaces (port 8033/TCP), orchestrates content safety detection by forwarding text to configurable detector services via REST, chunks text via gRPC chunker services, and coordinates generation through a TGIS or caikit-nlp gRPC backend. A separate health server (port 8034/TCP) provides unauthenticated health and info endpoints. The service supports optional TLS and mTLS on its ingress surface, passthrough of configurable client headers to downstream services, and rewriting of X-Forwarded-Access-Token headers to Authorization Bearer for downstream authentication. Two additional v2 endpoints for OpenAI-compatible chat and text completions detection are conditionally enabled when an OpenAI-compatible generation backend is configured. The orchestrator is built for multi-architecture deployment (amd64, ppc64le, s390x) on UBI 9 minimal base images. [source: Cargo.toml:1-7, config/config.yaml:1-70, src/server/routes.rs:62-108, src/args.rs:31-47]\n20:The orchestrator follows a middleware proxy pattern: it sits between API clients and multiple backend services (generation, detection, chunking), adding safety guardrails to the text generation pipeline. The axum HTTP framework handles inbound REST requests on port 8033, while tonic-generated gRPC clients communicate with downstream TGIS generation and caikit chunker services. Detector services are reached via reqwest REST clients. Each downstream service type supports independent TLS configuration through a named TLS map in the YAML config, allowing per-service certificate and CA bundles. [source: config/config.yaml:53-66, Cargo.toml:56-65, 85-89]\n24:Authentication is passthrough-based rather than enforced: configurable header names are forwarded from client requests to downstream services, and an optional X-Forwarded-Access-Token rewrite converts forwarded access tokens into Authorization Bearer headers for downstream consumption. The orchestrator itself does not validate tokens or enforce authorization policies; it delegates authentication to the downstream services and to the platform's ingress layer. TLS and mTLS on the inbound surface are optional, controlled by CLI flags and environment variables. [source: src/server/routes.rs:452-480, src/args.rs:43-47, config/config.yaml:67-70]\n26:The cryptographic stack uses rustls with the ring provider throughout (rustls, hyper-rustls, tokio-rustls, tonic TLS). Ring is not a FIPS-validated cryptographic provider, which means the service cannot claim FIPS compliance for its TLS operations. OpenSSL is present only in the build stage for protobuf compilation and is not installed in the release image. [source: Cargo.toml:33-34, 62-65, 81-83, 85-88, Dockerfile.konflux:17, 51-53]\n68:| /api/v1/task/classification-with-text-generation | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | classification with gen |\n69:| /api/v1/task/server-streaming-classification-with-text-generation | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | stream classification with gen |\n70:| /api/v2/chat/completions-detection | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | chat completions detection |\n71:| /api/v2/text/completions-detection | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | completions detection |\n72:| /api/v2/text/detection/chat | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | detect chat |\n73:| /api/v2/text/detection/content | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | detection content |\n74:| /api/v2/text/detection/context | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | detect context documents |\n75:| /api/v2/text/detection/generated | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | detect generated |\n76:| /api/v2/text/detection/stream-content | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | stream content detection |\n77:| /api/v2/text/generation-detection | POST | 8033/TCP | HTTP/HTTPS | Unknown | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers |  | generation with detection |\n108:| hyper-rustls | 0.27.7 | Yes | Unknown | Cargo package dependency |\n118:| rustls | 0.23.36 | Yes | runtime-security | Cargo package dependency |\n119:| rustls-pemfile | 2.2.0 | Yes | Unknown | Cargo package dependency |\n120:| rustls-pki-types | 1.13.2 | Yes | Unknown | Cargo package dependency |\n121:| rustls-webpki | 0.103.8 | Yes | Unknown | Cargo package dependency |\n127:| tokio-rustls | 0.26.4 | Yes | Unknown | Cargo package dependency |\n154:| guardrails-server | N/A (binary) | 8033/TCP | 8033 | HTTP/HTTPS | TLS 1.2+ (optional) | Passthrough headers, optional mTLS | Internal |\n159:| Name | Type | Hosts | Port | Protocol | Encryption | TLS Mode | Exposure |\n166:| Chunker services | 8085 | gRPC | TLS (optional, configurable) | None | Configured downstream grpc client |\n168:| Detector services | 8080 | HTTP/HTTPS | TLS (optional, configurable) | Bearer token (optional) | Configured downstream rest api client |\n187:| TLS server cert/key | kubernetes.io/tls | Rust HTTP server TLS | Platform operator / cert-manager | Unknown |\n188:| TLS client CA cert | Opaque | Rust HTTP server mTLS | Platform operator | Unknown |\n190:| Downstream TLS certs | Opaque | Downstream service TLS clients | Platform operator | Unknown |\n196:| /api/v1/*, /api/v2/* | POST | Header passthrough | Application-level filtering | Configured headers are forwarded to downstream services |\n198:| All endpoints | ALL | TLS / mTLS | Rust TLS acceptor | Optional server TLS and client certificate verification |\n205:| crypto-library | rustls | Rust TLS dependency is present; the cryptographic provider and FIPS mode require configuration or lockfile verification | dependency-signal |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"5fe0d461-ffed-4abd-aa62-e818ceb02073","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:26:11.172Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-989a457b5cd8a821","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
