e: final-stage base change to registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc for all ubi9-minimal-based images in the RHOAI image inventory (RHOAI-Build-Config rhoai-3.5 CSV, 153 relatedImages; organized local inventory); coordinate owning teams' tracking tickets; no builder image changes; ensure builds remain green.\nAC:\n- Every ubi9-minimal-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with final runtime stage on ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc, or has a filed OCP exception\n- Inside switched containers, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports DEFAULT:PQ and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` includes ML-KEM-512/768/1024 (OpenSSL-backed images)\n- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages unchanged\n- Build pipelines green for all switched images\n- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base; PQC hybrid key exchange is opportunistically negotiated so non-PQC clients continue via classic ECDHE\n- TLS handshake latency regression within the threshold defined with the Performance team (see perf validation)\nHLR: HLR-1 (P0), HLR-3 (P0)\nRisks: teams missing deadline without filing exceptions → weekly reminders and escalation (handled by compliance coordination).\n\n**E004** (Implementation):\nTitle: Switch rhel9-6-els-based images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal\nSimilar; gated on AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase; ~34 images (notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, mlserver).\nDepends on: the AIPCC availability confirmation (rebase committed date). If rebase not committed in time, affected images pivot to OCP exceptions.\nACs similar + precondition: AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) completed before adoption.\n\n**E005** (Implementation):\nTitle: PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination\nDescription: Creates and maintains the PQC Readiness Matrix (the strategy's \"to be created\" design doc) and runs the compliance coordination process through September 15, 2026: per-image routing (switch vs. exception), team tracking-ticket linkage, weekly reminders, escalat