e Review, Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, Documentation Support). Documentation Support is \"Pending human review\", not Yes — no docs-authoring epic generated; if it becomes Yes, add one.\n6. Inventory discrepancy: strategy counts 153 relatedImages (RHOAI 3.5 CSV) while 3.6-ea.1 architecture context analyzes 72 components — readiness matrix must reconcile.\n7. Priority note: performance validation is P1 (NFR-derived, pre-ship gate) while compliance epics are P0 — not an inversion.\n8. External timing risks: AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slip and variant non-availability → exceptions (tiered delivery).\n\nTiered delivery:\n- Tier 1 (independent): E001, E002, E003, E005, E006\n- Tier 2 (dependency-gated): E004 (rebase), BRANCH-A-E008 (variants), BRANCH-A-E009 (audit), E007 (after switches)\n\nConditional branches documentation:\n- Gate E001, outcome A (variants available before deadline, image names confirmed) → BRANCH-A-E008. Outcome B (not available) → no branch epic; affected images route to OCP exception path covered by the compliance coordination epic.\n- Gate E002, outcome A (OpenSSL-backed TLS) → BRANCH-A-E009. Outcome B (pure rustls) → no branch epic; exception path via compliance coordination.\n\nOK. Now also the summary frontmatter: parent_strat, epic_count=7, critical_path_length=3. No triage (full decomposition).\n\nWait, should epic_count include branches? \"may count either\" — 7 main-plan. In the body I'll clarify: 7 main-plan epics + 2 conditional branch epics.\n\nNow write everything. Let me write the summary body first.\n\nOne more check — the \"no cross-references to sibling epics by draft ID\" rule applies to epic bodies. The decomposition summary CAN use IDs (it's the plan). OK.\n\nAlso for epic bodies: \"Depends on\" phrasing in plain terms. E004: \"Depends on confirmation of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date (the AIPCC PQC base availability investigation outcome)\". Fine — descriptive, no ID.\n\nLet me write the files now. I'll do Write ca