{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ba89f75d-f38e-4988-a537-70684547a677","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-babae4c59330f5b6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-x6o5vcr1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8001 (Base image compliance — Post-quantum cryptography support)\n\nStrategy is a PQC base-image compliance coordination tracker for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 with a\nSeptember 15, 2026 deadline. It is NOT below-threshold: although effort-rated S, it spans all\nRHOAI component images (multiple components), all RHOAI component teams plus the AIPCC and\nDevOps/Build teams, and contains genuine unknowns (PQC Python/Node.js base variants, RHEL 9.8\nrebase date, trainer data cache TLS posture) whose answers change which downstream epics exist.\nIt is not documentation-only: the scope requires Containerfile final-stage changes and CI work.\nFull decomposition follows.\n\nStaff Engineer / SME Input: section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to apply.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| E001 | Confirm AIPCC PQC base image availability (Python/Node.js variants and RHEL 9.8 rebase date) | Investigation | AIPCC team | P0 |\n| E002 | Audit trainer data cache TLS stack (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust) | Investigation | Training Kubeflow | P0 |\n| E003 | Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc | Implementation | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n| E004 | Switch rhel9-6-els-based images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal | Implementation | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n| E005 | PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination | Implementation | AI Core Platform | P0 |\n| E006 | Automated PQC compliance CI scan for the RHOAI payload | Implementation | CI/CD | P0 |\n| E007 | TLS handshake performance validation for PQC-switched images | Implementation | PerfScale | P1 |\n| BRANCH-A-E008 | Switch Python/Node.js-based images to confirmed PQC base variants | Implementation (branch A of E001) | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n| BRANCH-A-E009 | Switch trainer data cache image to a PQC base | Implementation (branch A of E002) | Implementation → Training Kubeflow | P0 |\n\nMain plan: 7 epics (E001–E007) + 2 conditional branch epics. `epic_count` counts main-plan epics.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n  E001[\"E001 Investigation: AIPCC PQC base availability\"]\n  E002[\"E002 Investigation: trainer data cache TLS audit\"]\n  E003[\"E003 Implementation: ubi9-minimal family switch\"]\n  E004[\"E004 Implementation: rhel9-6-els family switch\"]\n  E005[\"E005 Implementation: readiness matrix + compliance coordination\"]\n  E006[\"E006 Implementation: PQC compliance CI scan\"]\n  E007[\"E007 Implementation: TLS handshake performance validation\"]\n  BRANCH_A_E008[\"BRANCH-A-E008 (conditional: variants available)\"]\n  BRANCH_A_E009[\"BRANCH-A-E009 (conditional: OpenSSL-backed TLS)\"]\n\n  E001 --> E004\n  E001 --> BRANCH_A_E008\n  E002 --> BRANCH_A_E009\n  E003 --> E007\n  E004 --> E007\n```\n\nRoots (no dependencies, start immediately — Tier 1): E001, E002, E003, E005, E006.\nMain-plan critical path: E001 → E004 → E007 (length 3).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation determines downstream scope/approach) | The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date (AIPCC-7258) determines whether the ~34 rhel9-6-els-based images can adopt `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` by September 15 or must pivot to OCP exceptions. True gate: `gated_by=E001`, action `rewrite`. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 3 + conditional branch (bounded outcome, 2 possibilities) | Whether PQC variants of python-311/312/python-312-minimal/nodejs-22 exist with committed delivery before September 15 decides whether a switch epic for those ~11 images exists at all. Outcome A → branch epic; outcome B → no branch, images route to the OCP-exception path already covered by E005. |\n| E002 → BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 3 + conditional branch (bounded outcome, 2 possibilities) | The trainer data cache TLS audit decides whether a base swap remediates that image (OpenSSL-backed) or an OCP exception with TLS-migration remediation plan is required (pure rustls). Outcome A → branch epic; outcome B → no branch, exception path via E005. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 13 (artifact dependency) | Performance validation measures the rebuilt PQC-switched images; the measurement work builds on the switched image artifact produced by the family switch. |\n| E004 → E007 | Rule 13 (artifact dependency) | Same: rhel9-els family switched images are a measured input to the performance validation. |\n| No edge E003 ↔ E004 | Rules 14/15 (parallel) | Different image families, different target bases, no shared artifacts — Tier 1 vs Tier 2 split (Step 5.5). |\n| No edge E003/E004 → E006 | Rule 10 philosophy (AC-gated, not DAG-coupled) | The CI scan is built in parallel; its \"all OpenSSL-backed images report DEFAULT:PQ\" pass criterion gates at execution time against whatever payload exists, exactly like the konflux \"build pipeline green\" AC pattern. Wiring switch → scan edges would serialize naturally-parallel work. |\n| No edge E001/E002 → E005 | Rule 4 boundary | The readiness matrix records pending outcomes and fills routing entries dynamically; coordination does not block on the investigations. |\n| No edge for AIPCC-7258 itself | Rule 21 (third party resolves → precondition, no epic) | The RHEL 9.8 rebase is executed by AIPCC under AIPCC-7258, outside this strategy's epic set; it is captured as a precondition AC on E004 plus the E001 gate. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics | Notes |\n|-----|----------|-------|-------|\n| All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 | P0 | E003, E004, BRANCH-A-E008, BRANCH-A-E009 (switch execution); E005 (accountability: every image switched or exception-filed, zero unaccounted); E006 (automated verification of AC-1) | Images that cannot switch are covered through the HLR-2 exception alternative (TrustyAI Java/NSS, fms-guardrails-orchestrator rustls+ring, trainer data cache if pure-Rust, Python/Node.js images if variants unavailable). |\n| Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a remediation plan | P0 | E005 | Filing itself is each team's own work (explicitly out of scope per strategy); E005 enforces and aggregates. |\n| PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage changes, no builder image change | P0 | E003, E004, BRANCH-A-E008, BRANCH-A-E009 (scope constraint + AC) | Constraint carried as AC on every switch epic. |\n| PQC-signed X.509 certificates (ML-DSA) | Deferred | — | Explicitly deferred by the strategy; no epic, no coverage required. |\n\nStrategy acceptance criteria coverage: AC-1 (crypto policy verification) → E006 (+ rebuild work in\nswitch epics); AC-2 (zero unaccounted images by September 15) → E005; AC-3 (tracking tickets\nlinked, aggregated view) → E005.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing structured tables (non-blocking):** Affected Components is prose (\"all RHOAI component\n   images\") and Impacted Teams is a bullet list, not tables. Decomposition follows the strategy's\n   own base-image family mapping. Per-image Containerfile execution is delegated to owning\n   component teams via tracking tickets linked to this strategy (the strategy's stated mechanism);\n   the family switch epics are coordination epics owned by the DevOps/Build team, whose stated\n   involvement is \"coordinate base image pipeline updates\".\n2. **Performance NFR lacks a numeric threshold** — flagged NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT in the strategy\n   (owner: PM + Performance team lead, due before Sprint 2 ends). Resolution does not change epic\n   structure, so it is carried