rable without it, so the strategy splits:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately):** E001, E002, E003 (~68 images on the confirmed\n  `ubi9-minimal-pqc` base), E005 (readiness matrix + compliance coordination), E006 (CI scan).\n- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated):** E004 (~34 images, gated by AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase / E001 outcome),\n  BRANCH-A-E008 (~11 images, gated by PQC variant availability), BRANCH-A-E009 (single image,\n  gated by the TLS audit), E007 (measures switched images from both family switches).\n\n## Conditional Branches\n\n- **Gate E001 (AIPCC PQC base availability), outcome A — variants available with committed delivery\n  before September 15, 2026:** `BRANCH-A-E008` switches the Python/Node.js-based images\n  (5× python-311 training variants + lmes-job, 4× python-312 training variants, 1×\n  python-312-minimal feature-server, 1× nodejs-22 dashboard). `gate_failure_impact: remove` —\n  if the variants are not available, this epic does not exist and those images file OCP exceptions\n  through the main-plan compliance coordination epic.\n- **Gate E001, outcome B — variants not available in time:** no branch epics; affected images route\n  to the OCP exception path covered by E005 (HLR-2). This outcome is fully accounted for by the\n  main plan.\n- **Gate E002 (trainer data cache TLS audit), outcome A — OpenSSL-backed (native-tls) stack:**\n  `BRANCH-A-E009` switches the trainer data cache image to the appropriate PQC base for its family.\n  `gate_failure_impact: remove` — if the stack is pure rustls+ring, a base swap cannot remediate it\n  and the owning team files an OCP exception with a TLS-migration remediation plan (covered by E005).\n- **Gate E002, outcome B — pure-Rust TLS stack:** no branch epics; exception path via E005.\n\nBranch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path; no main-plan epic lists a branch epic\nin its dependencies.\n\n## Component Mapping Log\n\nCanonical names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`; non-obvious mappin