{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6617275e-028e-4fb4-bdca-d6c2332b1612","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9fabf5fa970e41b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-x6o5vcr1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E002.md","content":"# Audit trainer data cache TLS stack (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust)\n\n## Description\n\nDetermines whether the trainer data cache's Rust TLS stack is OpenSSL-backed (native-tls) or a\npure-Rust stack (rustls+ring). This is the strategy's stated unknown for the component (\"Rust TLS\nposture unknown; audit spike RHOAIENG-7196\"). The outcome decides the remediation path: if TLS\noperations route through system OpenSSL, a PQC base image swap remediates the component; if the\nstack is pure rustls+ring, a base swap cannot provide ML-KEM and the owning team must file an OCP\nexception with a TLS-migration remediation plan.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the trainer data cache's TLS dependencies and configuration in its source repository\n  (dependency lockfile, TLS client setup, any bundled crypto provider)\n- Determine whether TLS operations route through system OpenSSL (native-tls) or a pure-Rust\n  provider (rustls+ring)\n- Assess whether ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange would be available after a PQC base image\n  swap under each outcome\n- Produce a remediation recommendation (base image switch vs OCP exception with TLS-migration\n  remediation plan) and hand it to the compliance coordination process\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The TLS stack classification (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust) is documented with evidence from the\n  component source (dependency inventory and TLS configuration)\n- ML-KEM hybrid key exchange capability after a base image swap is determined and documented for\n  the audited stack\n- A remediation path recommendation (switch vs OCP exception with remediation plan) is recorded\n  and handed to the compliance coordination process before the September 15, 2026 deadline\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — the audit decides\n  whether this image is remediated by a base switch.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply must file an OCP exception — the audit decides whether this\n  component takes the exception path.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88736,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"7144a616-e3ff-49f7-9bcd-fd962537c143","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:20.244Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
