{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b0c38271-7bd8-4297-a32e-a05de5be1010","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4651f477c66ebd6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-x6o5vcr1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E003.md","content":"# Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the PQC base image switch for the ~68 platform images currently built on\n`ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` (Go operators and most platform components), by changing only the final\nruntime stage of each image's Dockerfile/Containerfile to\n`registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` (confirmed available, reports `DEFAULT:PQ`). Per the\nstrategy, each owning component team executes its own image switch through tracking tickets linked\nto the parent strategy; this epic coordinates the family-wide switch, its build pipeline updates,\nand its completion verification.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Final runtime stage base change from `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` for\n  every ubi9-minimal-based runtime image in the RHOAI image inventory (RHOAI-Build-Config\n  rhoai-3.5 CSV relatedImages and the organized local image inventory)\n- No builder image changes — PQC enablement is runtime only\n- Coordinate the DevOps/Build pipeline and build-config updates for the family\n- Track each owning component team's switch ticket to completion; images whose teams cannot\n  complete by September 15, 2026 route to the OCP exception process\n- Verification of switched images via the automated payload compliance scan\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every ubi9-minimal-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with its final runtime stage\n  on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, or its owning team has filed an OCP exception with a remediation plan\n- Inside each switched (OpenSSL-backed) container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports\n  `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024\n- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages are unchanged\n- Build pipelines are green for all switched images\n- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base image; PQC hybrid key exchange\n  (X25519MLKEM768) is negotiated opportunistically, so non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work\n  via classic ECDHE\n- TLS handshake latency regression for switched images is within the threshold defined with the\n  Performance team (validated by the performance validation workstream)\n- On FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivating PQC is expected behavior and is not treated as\n  a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n  switch for the ubi9-minimal family (~68 images).\n- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of each\n  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is made.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Teams missing the September 15 deadline without filing exceptions creates an untracked\n  compliance gap — weekly reminders and leadership escalation are handled by the compliance\n  coordination workstream.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90233,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"2b596b4f-5c8e-4b06-bbc1-00a3108dc365","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:33.512Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
