before `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` is adopted\n  for this family\n- Every rhel9-6-els-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with its final runtime stage\n  on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or its owning team has filed an OCP exception with a remediation\n  plan\n- Inside each switched (OpenSSL-backed) container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports\n  `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024\n- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages are unchanged\n- Build pipelines are green for all switched images\n- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base image; PQC hybrid key exchange\n  is negotiated opportunistically, so non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE\n- TLS handshake latency regression for switched images is within the threshold defined with the\n  Performance team (validated by the performance validation workstream)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n  switch for the rhel9-6-els family (~34 images).\n- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of each\n  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is made.\n\n## Risks\n\n- AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips — gates RHEL9-ELS image adoption. Mitigation: monitor AIPCC-7258;\n  teams using rhel9-6-els may need OCP exceptions (fallback captured in the gate failure impact).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90233,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"ec3a1252-e978-437a-a64f-3b326d6a4e0a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:37:44.803Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
