{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cc304c66-44c2-4656-ace5-20367de497c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de3e1c00501212d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-x6o5vcr1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E005.md","content":"# PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination\n\n## Description\n\nCreates and maintains the PQC Readiness Matrix (the strategy's \"to be created\" design doc: PQC\nReadiness Matrix per component) and runs the compliance coordination process through the\nSeptember 15, 2026 deadline: per-image routing (switch vs OCP exception), component-team tracking\nticket linkage for OCP 5.0 aggregated visibility, weekly reminders, leadership escalation, and the\nzero-unaccounted-images guarantee. Exception filing itself is each team's own work (explicitly out\nof scope per the strategy); this epic tracks, enforces, and aggregates it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the PQC Readiness Matrix from the RHOAI image inventory (RHOAI-Build-Config rhoai-3.5 CSV\n  relatedImages and the organized local image inventory), reconciled against the RHOAI 3.6 payload;\n  per image record: current base, target PQC base, TLS stack, owning team, switch-or-exception\n  decision, linked tracking ticket, and status\n- Record TLS-stack routing for the known non-OpenSSL components: fms-guardrails-orchestrator\n  (rustls+ring — cannot inherit PQC from a base image), TrustyAI explainability service\n  (Java/NSS on openjdk-17-runtime — exception expected, JDK 29 September 2027), trainer data cache\n  (pending its TLS audit), dashboard nodejs-22 image (pending PQC variant availability)\n- Ensure every component team's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy for OCP 5.0\n  aggregated visibility\n- Enforce the exception process: teams unable to comply by September 15, 2026 file an OCP exception\n  via the OCPEXCEPT template documenting the component's TLS stack, why it cannot negotiate ML-KEM,\n  and a remediation plan\n- Weekly reminders to teams; escalation to leadership per the sync decision for teams with neither\n  a switch nor a filed exception\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The PQC Readiness Matrix exists and covers every image in the RHOAI image inventory with the\n  fields above; the 3.5 CSV inventory (153 relatedImages) is reconciled against the RHOAI 3.6\n  payload and discrepancies are documented\n- By September 15, 2026, every RHOAI component image has either (a) been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled\n  base image or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan\n  including the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero\n  unaccounted-for images remain\n- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy, providing an aggregated\n  compliance view for OCP 5.0\n- Exception remediation plans for non-OpenSSL components (e.g. rustls+ring, Java/NSS) address\n  ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange support\n- Teams at risk of missing the deadline without an exception receive weekly reminders; teams with\n  neither a switch nor an exception are escalated to leadership\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic provides the\n  accountability mechanism (every image switched or exception-filed; zero unaccounted images).\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a\n  remediation plan — this epic enforces and aggregates the exception process.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- PQC hybrid key exchange (X25519MLKEM768) is backwards-compatible with non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients\n  (confirmed, IETF hybrid key exchange draft).\n- FIPS + PQC on UBI9 are currently incompatible; on FIPS-mode clusters FIPS policy deactivates\n  PQC for this release — expected behavior, not a compliance failure (confirmed).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92095,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"0c2b88f3-32e2-4da9-817c-a2e2e922602d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:00.921Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
