{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cc304c66-44c2-4656-ace5-20367de497c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a04a35514d64863a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-x6o5vcr1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E006.md","content":"# Automated PQC compliance CI scan for the RHOAI payload\n\n## Description\n\nImplements the automated CI scan that measures the strategy's primary acceptance criterion across\nthe RHOAI 3.6 payload: verifying, per shipped image, that the active crypto policy is `DEFAULT:PQ`\nand that ML-KEM algorithms are available through system OpenSSL. This scan is scoped strictly to\ncrypto-policy and algorithm verification — TLS adherence scanning (TLS-scanner CI) is owned by the\nseparate Central TLS Profile strategy and is out of scope here.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A CI job that scans the RHOAI 3.6 payload images and, inside each OpenSSL-backed image, executes\n  `update-crypto-policies --show` (expecting `DEFAULT:PQ`) and `openssl list -kem-algorithms`\n  (expecting ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024)\n- Per-image compliance reporting across the payload, suitable for tracking switch completion and\n  exception coverage over time\n- Handling for components using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS): reported as\n  exception-covered rather than failed, matching the acceptance criterion's scope note\n- Reporting expectation that on FIPS-mode clusters FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release —\n  `DEFAULT:PQ` being non-functional there is not a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The scan runs in CI across the RHOAI 3.6 payload and produces a per-image compliance report\n- Every OpenSSL-backed image in the payload reports `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy and lists\n  ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 in `openssl list -kem-algorithms`\n- Non-OpenSSL components are reported as exception-covered (linked to the OCP exception\n  tracking), not as scan failures\n- The FIPS-mode caveat is documented in the scan's reporting so FIPS-cluster results are\n  interpreted correctly\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n  automated measurement (\"measured by automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload\") for that\n  requirement.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The scan is built in parallel with the image switch work: it verifies whatever payload exists at\n  execution time; its green state across all OpenSSL-backed images is the terminal verification of\n  the strategy's primary acceptance criterion.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92095,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"cd6d71d4-997f-4055-a919-c606da6af56c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:10.016Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
