e image\n  families, with pre-switch baselines\n- Measured regressions are within the agreed threshold, or a documented remediation plan exists\n  for each exceeding image\n- Confirmation that HA characteristics are unchanged by the base image switch\n- The go/no-go report is delivered before RHOAI 3.6 ships\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- No HLR maps directly to this epic. It derives from the strategy's Non-Functional Requirements\n  (Performance: handshake regression measurement required before ship; Availability: no HA\n  characteristic changes) and the Performance Team Support prerequisite. Priority P1 reflects the\n  NFR-derived, pre-ship gate nature of the work.\n\n## Dependencies (plain terms)\n\n- Requires the switched images produced by the ubi9-minimal family switch and the rhel9-6-els\n  family switch (measurements are taken on the rebuilt images).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":93834,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-813da0bdcbbe65c6","agent_id":"a807aa13f2f9a62d7","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"45a6ee90-54c9-46fa-b36d-64e7f87e6569","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:38:22.092Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
