{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af3f1226aa9517a4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm AIPCC PQC base image availability (Python/Node.js variants and RHEL\n4\t  9.8 rebase date)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: AIPCC Productization\n7\tteam: AIPCC team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Confirm AIPCC PQC base image availability (Python/Node.js variants and RHEL 9.8 rebase date)\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves the strategy's external base-image unknowns with the AIPCC team (tracked as spike\n31\tRHOAIENG-7195): whether PQC-enabled variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`,\n32\t`ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` will exist — with confirmed registry image names —\n33\tbefore the September 15, 2026 deadline, and the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase\n34\t(AIPCC-7258) that gates adoption of the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` base. The outcome determines\n35\twhether the Python/Node.js-based images (~11) can be switched or must file OCP exceptions, and\n36\twhether the ~34 rhel9-6-els-based images can adopt the RHEL9-ELS PQC base in time or pivot to\n37\texceptions.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Confirm existence and exact registry names of PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`,\n42\t  `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` (aligned with spike\n43\t  RHOAIENG-7195 and the AIPCC team)\n44\t- Obtain committed delivery dates for those variants relative to September 15, 2026\n45\t- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258), which gates RHEL9-ELS\n46\t  PQC base image adoption for the rhel9-6-els image family\n47\t- Verify the PQC behavior of any delivered variant locally (pulled container image reports\n48\t  `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy and exposes ML-KEM algorithms through system OpenSSL)\n49\t- Record outcomes and provide a go/no-go signal per image family; escalate if no committed\n50\t  variant date exists by early September 2026 (per the strategy's risk mitigation)\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Confirmed image names (or confirmed non-existence) for each of the four requested base variants,\n55\t  each with a committed delivery date, documented and communicated to the affected component teams\n56\t- The RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date is documented and a go/no-go signal is provided for RHEL9-ELS\n57\t  PQC base adoption by September 15, 2026\n58\t- Any delivered PQC base variant is verified to report `DEFAULT:PQ` via `update-crypto-policies --show`\n59\t  and to expose ML-KEM-512/768/1024 via `openssl list -kem-algorithms` when run locally\n60\t- Escalation is triggered if no committed date for the Python/Node.js variants exists by early\n61\t  September 2026\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this investigation\n66\t  enables the switch-vs-exception decision for the Python/Node.js-based images and the\n67\t  rhel9-6-els-based image family.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0a326a4c4a3969","agent_id":"acc1233cc06bd6f35","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"086b929a-b410-4bf8-8164-fc98eb82325a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:41:54.629Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af3f1226aa9517a4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
