executes its own image switch through\n45\ttracking tickets linked to the parent strategy; this epic coordinates the family-wide switch.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Final runtime stage base change from `rhel9-6-els/rhel:9.6-*` to `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for\n50\t  every rhel9-6-els-based runtime image in the RHOAI image inventory\n51\t- No builder image changes — PQC enablement is runtime only\n52\t- Confirm the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) has completed before adopting the new base\n53\t  (external precondition; its committed date is resolved by the AIPCC base availability\n54\t  investigation)\n55\t- Coordinate the DevOps/Build pipeline and build-config updates for the family\n56\t- Track each owning component team's switch ticket to completion; images whose teams cannot\n57\t  complete by September 15, 2026 route to the OCP exception process\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) is completed before `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` is adopted\n62\t  for this family\n63\t- Every rhel9-6-els-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with its final runtime stage\n64\t  on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or its owning team has filed an OCP exception with a remediation\n65\t  plan\n66\t- Inside each switched (OpenSSL-backed) container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports\n67\t  `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024\n68\t- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages are unchanged\n69\t- Build pipelines are green for all switched images\n70\t- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base image; PQC hybrid key exchange\n71\t  is negotiated opportunistically, so non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE\n72\t- TLS handshake latency regression for switched images is within the threshold defined with the\n73\t  Performance team (validated by the performance validation workstream)\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n78\t  switch for the rhel9-6-els family (~34 images).\n79\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of each\n80\t  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is made.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks\n83\t\n84\t- AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips — gates RHEL9-ELS image adoption. Mitigation: monitor AIPCC-7258;\n85\t  teams using rhel9-6-els may need OCP exceptions (fallback captured in the gate failure impact).\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0a326a4c4a3969","agent_id":"acc1233cc06bd6f35","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"9a1ecd87-9779-4b4d-8242-75bc5a93fde1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:41:57.350Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e442fb4952698b5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
