{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82964d0b4f1af9a9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E006\n3\ttitle: Automated PQC compliance CI scan for the RHOAI payload\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: CI/CD\n6\tteam: CI/CD\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Automated PQC compliance CI scan for the RHOAI payload\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tImplements the automated CI scan that measures the strategy's primary acceptance criterion across\n34\tthe RHOAI 3.6 payload: verifying, per shipped image, that the active crypto policy is `DEFAULT:PQ`\n35\tand that ML-KEM algorithms are available through system OpenSSL. This scan is scoped strictly to\n36\tcrypto-policy and algorithm verification — TLS adherence scanning (TLS-scanner CI) is owned by the\n37\tseparate Central TLS Profile strategy and is out of scope here.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- A CI job that scans the RHOAI 3.6 payload images and, inside each OpenSSL-backed image, executes\n42\t  `update-crypto-policies --show` (expecting `DEFAULT:PQ`) and `openssl list -kem-algorithms`\n43\t  (expecting ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024)\n44\t- Per-image compliance reporting across the payload, suitable for tracking switch completion and\n45\t  exception coverage over time\n46\t- Handling for components using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS): reported as\n47\t  exception-covered rather than failed, matching the acceptance criterion's scope note\n48\t- Reporting expectation that on FIPS-mode clusters FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release —\n49\t  `DEFAULT:PQ` being non-functional there is not a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The scan runs in CI across the RHOAI 3.6 payload and produces a per-image compliance report\n54\t- Every OpenSSL-backed image in the payload reports `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy and lists\n55\t  ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 in `openssl list -kem-algorithms`\n56\t- Non-OpenSSL components are reported as exception-covered (linked to the OCP exception\n57\t  tracking), not as scan failures\n58\t- The FIPS-mode caveat is documented in the scan's reporting so FIPS-cluster results are\n59\t  interpreted correctly\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n64\t  automated measurement (\"measured by automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload\") for that\n65\t  requirement.\n66\t\n67\t## Notes\n68\t\n69\t- The scan is built in parallel with the image switch work: it verifies whatever payload exists at\n70\t  execution time; its green state across all OpenSSL-backed images is the terminal verification of\n71\t  the strategy's primary acceptance criterion.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf0a326a4c4a3969","agent_id":"acc1233cc06bd6f35","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"92368acf-7bd7-4413-b7c6-79748c39d62c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:42:02.051Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82964d0b4f1af9a9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
