{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b83650cf2a35a107","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8001 (Base image compliance — Post-quantum cryptography support)\n10\t\n11\tStrategy is a PQC base-image compliance coordination tracker for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 with a\n12\tSeptember 15, 2026 deadline. It is NOT below-threshold: although effort-rated S, it spans all\n13\tRHOAI component images (multiple components), all RHOAI component teams plus the AIPCC and\n14\tDevOps/Build teams, and contains genuine unknowns (PQC Python/Node.js base variants, RHEL 9.8\n15\trebase date, trainer data cache TLS posture) whose answers change which downstream epics exist.\n16\tIt is not documentation-only: the scope requires Containerfile final-stage changes and CI work.\n17\tFull decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\tStaff Engineer / SME Input: section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to apply.\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n25\t| E001 | Confirm AIPCC PQC base image availability (Python/Node.js variants and RHEL 9.8 rebase date) | Investigation | AIPCC team | P0 |\n26\t| E002 | Audit trainer data cache TLS stack (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust) | Investigation | Training Kubeflow | P0 |\n27\t| E003 | Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc | Implementation | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n28\t| E004 | Switch rhel9-6-els-based images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal | Implementation | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n29\t| E005 | PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination | Implementation | AI Core Platform | P0 |\n30\t| E006 | Automated PQC compliance CI scan for the RHOAI payload | Implementation | CI/CD | P0 |\n31\t| E007 | TLS handshake performance validation for PQC-switched images | Implementation | PerfScale | P1 |\n32\t| BRANCH-A-E008 | Switch Python/Node.js-based images to confirmed PQC base variants | Implementation (branch A of E001) | DevOps/Build team | P0 |\n33\t| BRANCH-A-E009 | Switch trainer data cache image to a PQC base | Implementation (branch A of E002) | Training Kubeflow | P0 |\n34\t\n35\tMain plan: 7 epics (E001–E007) + 2 conditional branch epics. `epic_count` counts main-plan epics.\n36\t\n37\t## Dependency DAG\n38\t\n39\t```mermaid\n40\tgraph TD\n41\t  E001[\"E001 Investigation: AIPCC PQC base availability\"]\n42\t  E002[\"E002 Investigation: trainer data cache TLS audit\"]\n43\t  E003[\"E003 Implementation: ubi9-minimal family switch\"]\n44\t  E004[\"E004 Implementation: rhel9-6-els family switch\"]\n45\t  E005[\"E005 Implementation: readiness matrix + compliance coordination\"]\n46\t  E006[\"E006 Implementation: PQC compliance CI scan\"]\n47\t  E007[\"E007 Implementation: TLS handshake performance validation\"]\n48\t  BRANCH_A_E008[\"BRANCH-A-E008 (conditional: variants available)\"]\n49\t  BRANCH_A_E009[\"BRANCH-A-E009 (conditional: OpenSSL-backed TLS)\"]\n50\t\n51\t  E001 --> E004\n52\t  E001 --> BRANCH_A_E008\n53\t  E002 --> BRANCH_A_E009\n54\t  E003 --> E007\n55\t  E004 --> E007\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tRoots (no dependencies, start immediately — Tier 1): E001, E002, E003, E005, E006.\n59\tMain-plan critical path: E001 → E004 → E007 (length 3).\n60\t\n61\t## DAG Justification\n62\t\n63\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n64\t|------|------|-----------|\n65\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation determines downstream scope/approach) | The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date (AIPCC-7258) determines whether the ~34 rhel9-6-els-based images can adopt `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` by September 15 or must pivot to OCP exceptions. True gate: `gated_by=E001`, action `rewrite`. |\n66\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 | Rule 3 + conditional branch (bounded outcome, 2 possibilities) | Whether PQC variants of python-311/312/python-312-minimal/nodejs-22 exist with committed delivery before September 15 decides whether a switch epic for those ~11 images exists at all. Outcome A → branch epic; outcome B → no branch, images route to the OCP-exception path already covered by E005. |\n67\t| E002 → BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 3 + conditional branch (bounded outcome, 2 possibilities) | The trainer data cache TLS audit decides whether a base swap remediates that image (OpenSSL-backed) or an OCP exception with TLS-migration remediation plan is required (pure rustls). Outcome A → branch epic; outcome B → no branch, exception path via E005. |\n68\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 13 (artifact dependency) | Performance validation measures the rebuilt PQC-switched images; the measurement work builds on the switched image artifact produced by the family switch. |\n69\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 13 (artifact dependency) | Same: rhel9-els family switched images are a measured input to the performance validation. |\n70\t| No edge E003 ↔ E004 | Rules 14/15 (parallel) | Different image families, different target bases, no shared artifacts — Tier 1 vs Tier 2 split (Step 5.5). |\n71\t| No edge E003/E004 → E006 | Rule 10 philosophy (AC-gated, not DAG-coupled) | The CI scan is built in parallel; its \"all OpenSSL-backed images report DEFAULT:PQ\" pass criterion gates at execution time against whatever payload exists, exactly like the konflux \"build pipeline green\" AC pattern. Wiring switch → scan edges would serialize naturally-parallel work. |\n72\t| No edge E001/E002 → E005 | Rule 4 boundary | The readiness matrix records pending outcomes and fills routing entries dynamically; coordination does not block on the investigations. |\n73\t| No edge for AIPCC-7258 itself | Rule 21 (third party resolves → precondition, no epic) | The RHEL 9.8 rebase is executed by AIPCC under AIPCC-7258, outside this strategy's epic set; it is captured as a precondition AC on E004 plus the E001 gate. |\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceabili