{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4308cd915dc6a5f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-A-E008\n3\ttitle: Switch Python/Node.js-based images to confirmed PQC base variants\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If PQC variants of the Python and Node.js bases are not available\n16\t    with committed delivery before September 15 2026, this epic is removed; the affected\n17\t    teams file OCP exceptions with remediation plans tracked by the compliance coordination\n18\t    process.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 0\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Switch Python/Node.js-based images to confirmed PQC base variants\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional branch — exists only if the AIPCC PQC base availability investigation confirms outcome\n40\tA: PQC variants of the Python and Node.js bases are available (or committed) before the\n41\tSeptember 15, 2026 deadline. Delivers the PQC base image switch for the ~11 images currently built\n42\ton `ubi9/python-311` (5 images — training variants, lmes-job), `ubi9/python-312` (4 images —\n43\ttraining variants), `ubi9/python-312-minimal` (1 image — feature-server), and `ubi9/nodejs-22`\n44\t(1 image — dashboard, largely behind a Go proxy), by changing only the final runtime stage of each\n45\timage to the confirmed PQC variant. Each owning component team executes its own image switch\n46\tthrough tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy; this epic coordinates the family-wide\n47\tswitch.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Final runtime stage base change to the confirmed PQC variant for every python-311-,\n52\t  python-312-, python-312-minimal-, and nodejs-22-based runtime image in the RHOAI image inventory,\n53\t  using the exact variant image names confirmed by the AIPCC availability investigation\n54\t- No builder image changes — PQC enablement is runtime only\n55\t- Coordinate the DevOps/Build pipeline and build-config updates for the family\n56\t- Track each owning component team's switch ticket to completion; images whose teams cannot\n57\t  complete by September 15, 2026 route to the OCP exception process\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Every Python/Node.js-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with its final runtime\n62\t  stage on the confirmed PQC base variant, or its owning team has filed an OCP exception with a\n63\t  remediation plan\n64\t- Inside each switched (OpenSSL-backed) container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports\n65\t  `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024\n66\t- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages are unchanged\n67\t- Build pipelines are green for all switched images\n68\t- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base image; PQC hybrid key exchange\n69\t  is negotiated opportunistically, so non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n74\t  switch for the Python/Node.js-based image family (~11 images).\n75\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of each\n76\t  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is made.\n77\t\n78\t## Risks\n79\t\n80\t- PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs not available in time — in that case this epic is removed\n81\t  and the affected teams file OCP exceptions instead (gate failure impact).\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6679c9c492244df","agent_id":"ade7f978058bfdf0c","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"9ac1ff9e-7aac-433e-aa8a-029dafcea860","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:47:40.662Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4308cd915dc6a5f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
