{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b2d9da478c0707","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E002\n3\ttitle: Audit trainer data cache TLS stack (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Training Kubeflow\n6\tteam: Training Kubeflow\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Audit trainer data cache TLS stack (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermines whether the trainer data cache's Rust TLS stack is OpenSSL-backed (native-tls) or a\n30\tpure-Rust stack (rustls+ring). This is the strategy's stated unknown for the component (\"Rust TLS\n31\tposture unknown; audit spike RHOAIENG-7196\"). The outcome decides the remediation path: if TLS\n32\toperations route through system OpenSSL, a PQC base image swap remediates the component; if the\n33\tstack is pure rustls+ring, a base swap cannot provide ML-KEM and the owning team must file an OCP\n34\texception with a TLS-migration remediation plan.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Inspect the trainer data cache's TLS dependencies and configuration in its source repository\n39\t  (dependency lockfile, TLS client setup, any bundled crypto provider)\n40\t- Determine whether TLS operations route through system OpenSSL (native-tls) or a pure-Rust\n41\t  provider (rustls+ring)\n42\t- Assess whether ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange would be available after a PQC base image\n43\t  swap under each outcome\n44\t- Produce a remediation recommendation (base image switch vs OCP exception with TLS-migration\n45\t  remediation plan) and hand it to the compliance coordination process\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- The TLS stack classification (OpenSSL-backed vs pure-Rust) is documented with evidence from the\n50\t  component source (dependency inventory and TLS configuration)\n51\t- ML-KEM hybrid key exchange capability after a base image swap is determined and documented for\n52\t  the audited stack\n53\t- A remediation path recommendation (switch vs OCP exception with remediation plan) is recorded\n54\t  and handed to the compliance coordination process before the September 15, 2026 deadline\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — the audit decides\n59\t  whether this image is remediated by a base switch.\n60\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply must file an OCP exception — the audit decides whether this\n61\t  component takes the exception path.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92622886643e7d18","agent_id":"a1f7a18ed15aee595","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"d9c74f93-2cc4-4f8b-a50b-32b8c676a741","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:50:40.826Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1b2d9da478c0707","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001"}
