{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b05d65f47296d116","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n3\ttitle: Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers the PQC base image switch for the ~68 platform images currently built on\n34\t`ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` (Go operators and most platform components), by changing only the final\n35\truntime stage of each image's Dockerfile/Containerfile to\n36\t`registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` (confirmed available, reports `DEFAULT:PQ`). Per the\n37\tstrategy, each owning component team executes its own image switch through tracking tickets linked\n38\tto the parent strategy; this epic coordinates the family-wide switch, its build pipeline updates,\n39\tand its completion verification.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Final runtime stage base change from `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` for\n44\t  every ubi9-minimal-based runtime image in the RHOAI image inventory (RHOAI-Build-Config\n45\t  rhoai-3.5 CSV relatedImages and the organized local image inventory)\n46\t- No builder image changes — PQC enablement is runtime only\n47\t- Coordinate the DevOps/Build pipeline and build-config updates for the family\n48\t- Track each owning component team's switch ticket to completion; images whose teams cannot\n49\t  complete by September 15, 2026 route to the OCP exception process\n50\t- Verification of switched images via the automated payload compliance scan\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Every ubi9-minimal-based runtime image in the inventory is rebuilt with its final runtime stage\n55\t  on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, or its owning team has filed an OCP exception with a remediation plan\n56\t- Inside each switched (OpenSSL-backed) container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports\n57\t  `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024\n58\t- Only the final runtime stage changed; builder stages are unchanged\n59\t- Build pipelines are green for all switched images\n60\t- Rollback: each switched image can be reverted to its prior base image; PQC hybrid key exchange\n61\t  (X25519MLKEM768) is negotiated opportunistically, so non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work\n62\t  via classic ECDHE\n63\t- TLS handshake latency regression for switched images is within the threshold defined with the\n64\t  Performance team (validated by the performance validation workstream)\n65\t- On FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivating PQC is expected behavior and is not treated as\n66\t  a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic delivers the\n71\t  switch for the ubi9-minimal family (~68 images).\n72\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of each\n73\t  Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is made.\n74\t\n75\t## Risks\n76\t\n77\t- Teams missing the September 15 deadline without filing exceptions creates an untracked\n78\t  compliance gap — weekly reminders and leadership escalation are handled by the compliance\n79\t  coordination workstream.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92622886643e7d18","agent_id":"a1f7a18ed15aee595","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"dcfa3917-7383-4728-a308-8bd63e14d04c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:50:41.627Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b05d65f47296d116","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001"}
