{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9beae4805a44eece","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: AI Core Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tCreates and maintains the PQC Readiness Matrix (the strategy's \"to be created\" design doc: PQC\n34\tReadiness Matrix per component) and runs the compliance coordination process through the\n35\tSeptember 15, 2026 deadline: per-image routing (switch vs OCP exception), component-team tracking\n36\tticket linkage for OCP 5.0 aggregated visibility, weekly reminders, leadership escalation, and the\n37\tzero-unaccounted-images guarantee. Exception filing itself is each team's own work (explicitly out\n38\tof scope per the strategy); this epic tracks, enforces, and aggregates it.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Build the PQC Readiness Matrix from the RHOAI image inventory (RHOAI-Build-Config rhoai-3.5 CSV\n43\t  relatedImages and the organized local image inventory), reconciled against the RHOAI 3.6 payload;\n44\t  per image record: current base, target PQC base, TLS stack, owning team, switch-or-exception\n45\t  decision, linked tracking ticket, and status\n46\t- Record TLS-stack routing for the known non-OpenSSL components: fms-guardrails-orchestrator\n47\t  (rustls+ring — cannot inherit PQC from a base image), TrustyAI explainability service\n48\t  (Java/NSS on openjdk-17-runtime — exception expected, JDK 29 September 2027), trainer data cache\n49\t  (pending its TLS audit), dashboard nodejs-22 image (pending PQC variant availability)\n50\t- Ensure every component team's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy for OCP 5.0\n51\t  aggregated visibility\n52\t- Enforce the exception process: teams unable to comply by September 15, 2026 file an OCP exception\n53\t  via the OCPEXCEPT template documenting the component's TLS stack, why it cannot negotiate ML-KEM,\n54\t  and a remediation plan\n55\t- Weekly reminders to teams; escalation to leadership per the sync decision for teams with neither\n56\t  a switch nor a filed exception\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The PQC Readiness Matrix exists and covers every image in the RHOAI image inventory with the\n61\t  fields above; the 3.5 CSV inventory (153 relatedImages) is reconciled against the RHOAI 3.6\n62\t  payload and discrepancies are documented\n63\t- By September 15, 2026, every RHOAI component image has either (a) been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled\n64\t  base image or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan\n65\t  including the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero\n66\t  unaccounted-for images remain\n67\t- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy, providing an aggregated\n68\t  compliance view for OCP 5.0\n69\t- Exception remediation plans for non-OpenSSL components (e.g. rustls+ring, Java/NSS) address\n70\t  ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange support\n71\t- Teams at risk of missing the deadline without an exception receive weekly reminders; teams with\n72\t  neither a switch nor an exception are escalated to leadership\n73\t- Routing entries in the readiness matrix for images whose remediation route is determined by the\n74\t  pending investigations — the Python/Node.js-based images (pending the AIPCC PQC base variant\n75\t  availability confirmation) and the trainer data cache (pending its TLS stack audit) — are\n76\t  finalized from those investigation outcomes when they conclude, and each such image's matrix\n77\t  entry reflects the resulting switch-or-exception decision\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic provides the\n82\t  accountability mechanism (every image switched or exception-filed; zero unaccounted images).\n83\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a\n84\t  remediation plan — this epic enforces and aggregates the exception process.\n85\t\n86\t## Assumptions\n87\t\n88\t- PQC hybrid key exchange (X25519MLKEM768) is backwards-compatible with non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients\n89\t  (confirmed, IETF hybrid key exchange draft).\n90\t- FIPS + PQC on UBI9 are currently incompatible; on FIPS-mode clusters FIPS policy deactivates\n91\t  PQC for this release — expected behavior, not a compliance failure (confirmed).\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92622886643e7d18","agent_id":"a1f7a18ed15aee595","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"afd00080-fcda-4c62-8773-3a9eb98b8186","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:50:46.126Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9beae4805a44eece","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001"}
