{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6a888825404d6e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E007\n3\ttitle: TLS handshake performance validation for PQC-switched images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: PerfScale\n6\tteam: PerfScale\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E004\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 0\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: -1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 0\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Low\n25\tai_implementability_score: -1\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# TLS handshake performance validation for PQC-switched images\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tDefines the strategy's missing numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold (the Performance\n36\tNFR is flagged NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT, owner: PM + Performance team lead) and measures handshake\n37\tlatency on the PQC-switched RHOAI runtime images against pre-switch baselines before ship. The\n38\tPerformance Team support prerequisite (\"TLS handshake latency regression measurement needed before\n39\tship\") is satisfied by this work. Measurements are performed on the switched images produced by\n40\tthe base image family switches (ubi9-minimal family and rhel9-6-els family), so this work runs\n41\tafter those switches.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Confirm the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold with the PM and Performance team\n46\t  lead (references: PSASTRAT-7170 Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome; Chrome ~10% maximum TLS\n47\t  handshake time regression as an interim comparison point)\n48\t- Measure TLS handshake latency (PQC hybrid X25519MLKEM768 vs classic ECDHE) for PQC-switched\n49\t  RHOAI runtime images against their pre-switch baselines\n50\t- Report per-image-family go/no-go against the threshold; document remediation for any image\n51\t  exceeding it\n52\t- Verify that the base image switch does not change HA characteristics (no additional replicas\n53\t  required)\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold is defined and signed off by the PM and\n58\t  Performance team lead (resolving the NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT flag before Sprint 2 ends)\n59\t- TLS handshake latency measurements exist for the PQC-switched images of both switched base image\n60\t  families, with pre-switch baselines\n61\t- Measured regressions are within the agreed threshold, or a documented remediation plan exists\n62\t  for each exceeding image\n63\t- Confirmation that HA characteristics are unchanged by the base image switch\n64\t- The go/no-go report is delivered before RHOAI 3.6 ships\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- No HLR maps directly to this epic. It derives from the strategy's Non-Functional Requirements\n69\t  (Performance: handshake regression measurement required before ship; Availability: no HA\n70\t  characteristic changes) and the Performance Team Support prerequisite. Priority P1 reflects the\n71\t  NFR-derived, pre-ship gate nature of the work.\n72\t\n73\t## Dependencies (plain terms)\n74\t\n75\t- Requires the switched images produced by the ubi9-minimal family switch and the rhel9-6-els\n76\t  family switch (measurements are taken on the rebuilt images).\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92622886643e7d18","agent_id":"a1f7a18ed15aee595","session_id":"ca054b9d-00ed-4360-a728-320abe6368d2","uuid":"fcff1f18-88e7-4b21-b8bd-23754d26d545","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:50:48.108Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c6a888825404d6e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001"}
